   \"type\": \"number_disagrees\",\n          \"quote\": \"Scraped off the floor of the envelope, and it pays like the floor.\",\n          \"evidence\": \"[2.6a] \\\"One continuous orbital band, 50,000 m to 280,000 m, with a value gradient ... a piece's value multiplier interpolates on its altitude from 1.0 at the floor to 5.5 at the ceiling.\\\" Loot table: bent_truss_section 30 kg | 67,000 m; torn_foil_blanket sits lower at 52,500 m.\",\n          \"cites\": [\n            \"2.6a\"\n          ],\n          \"why\": \"The floor is 50,000 m and pays 1.0x. This piece is 17 km above it at 67,000 m, the fourth row up, paying about 1.33x — low in the band, but not the floor and not floor money.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"corrected\": {\n        \"flavour\": \"A dozen thin rusty bars crossed at every angle in a flat mat, speckled brown where the coating gave up. Low in the envelope, and it pays what low pays.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"severed_boom_mast\",\n      \"verdict\": \"revise\",\n      \"issues\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"contradicts_gdd\",\n          \"quote\": \"Bulky in the hold, and this high up every kilo of it pays.\",\n          \"evidence\": \"[4.3] \\\"Size classes, fragile flag, compactor, crane magnet, oversized junk. All exist to serve the endgame. Every piece is one slot; the module is simply very heavy.\\\" Loot table: severed_boom_mast 165 kg | 234,000 m | oversized.\",\n          \"cites\": [\n            \"4.3\"\n          ],\n          \"why\": \"The collision is between the document and the table, not inside the writing: §4.3 cut size classes and fixed every piece at one slot, and the table still carries a size_class column with oversized rows. Raising it once here for the whole set. The table is what the game spawns, so the bulk stays in the fiction; what does not stay is \\\"in the hold\\\", which asserts variable cargo space the passage explicitly closed.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"corrected\": {\n        \"flavour\": \"A braided strand running long and twisted, frayed open into a bristly knot where it was cut. Unwieldy for its weight, and this high up every kilo of it pays.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shattered_cryo_dewar\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"issues\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_command_module_hatch\",\n      \"verdict\": \"revise\",\n      \"issues\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"wrong_voice\",\n          \"quote\": \"a highlight on the upper corner and nothing else in the cell\",\n          \"evidence\": \"[1c] \\\"Pillars: #Thematic — Scrapyard Spaceflight, blue-collar handmade spacecraft.\\\"\",\n          \"cites\": [\n            \"1c\"\n          ],\n          \"why\": \"\\\"the cell\\\" is the contact sheet's grid square — production language about the sprite sheet, not a place in the world. A player reading this in the hold is being told about an art asset.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"corrected\": {\n        \"flavour\": \"One small hex ring, face-on, hole through the middle, a highlight on the upper corner and nothing else to it. It will not take a knock, and it is absurd that a nut from up here outsells a panel from down low.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"armstrongs_module\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"issues\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":93809,"ttft_stream_ms":1285,"time_to_request_ms":229,"type":"result","duration_ms":106594,"uuid":"8d6580fa-3c78-4b94-9966-2d18322bc3bb"}
